  "id": "piagetian-theory",
  "term": "Piagetian theory",
  "definition": "Piagetian theory is a developmental framework that describes children’s understanding as gradually being built from their early actions and interactions with people and objects. In the moral domain, it includes an action-based level of development that comes before heteronomous and autonomous moral reasoning.",
